{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1793377027,"nonce":"rr24FiTSMeh4JskODQj/G0J/nN0=","message":"Correction to the survey above: Ashui's side is not a blocker. The data is all in Ashui and readable at macro time by a provider living in Ashui (private statics are fine from inside the class):\n- tags: Hxx TEXT_TAGS / BOX_TAGS / FLOW_TAGS / BUILT_IN_CLASSES; events: HANDLERS (name =\u003e event type);\n- layout attributes: ashui.layout.Prop; CSS properties: Properties handlers map (Properties.known);\n- component props: the component classes' own fields, which Rayzor's typer already resolves;\n- Tw: vocabulary() returns an enumerable Map covering the bulk, plus STATES for variants.\nOnly a few Tw rules sit outside that map and need listing as patterns/snippets or hoisting into tables: keywordCss's inline value lists, glassCss, colour opacity `/N`, arbitrary `[clip-path:...]`.\nWhat is missing is only the channel: one small public provider function per syntax in Ashui, plus the Rayzor work (metadata channel, tolerant markup scanner, textEdit/triggers). Rayzor work remains the first step.","files":null}]}